      "body": "## Motivation\n\nOn `amd_march`, the DSA indexer top-k kernels in `include/hip/dsa_topk_coop.cuh` hard-code `kWaveSize = 64`. On RDNA (wave32), every wave-level scan and ballot in them is wrong, so `fast_topk*` / `fast_topk_transform*` / `deepseek_v4_topk*` return wrong indices.\n\nOn unmodified `amd_march`, `tests/test_topk.py` gives `157 failed, 5 passed` on both gfx1100 (W7900D) and gfx1201 (R9700), for example:\n\n```\nE   AssertionError: wrong_values=92, max_permit_error=5\n```\n\n`main` already fixed this in #41687. That PR selects `kWaveSize` by arch macro and traps if the launched wavefront size disagrees. This PR is a clean `git cherry-pick -x` of it onto `amd_march`, with no conflicts and the original authorship kept. Part of the RDNA plan in #46900.\n\n## Modifications\n\nCherry-pick of 682f4ef32f (#41687), `include/hip/dsa_topk_coop.cuh` only (+20):\n\n- `kWaveSize = 32` for `__GFX10__` / `__GFX11__` / `__GFX12__`, and 64 otherwise.\n- `check_wave_size()` traps when `__builtin_amdgcn_wavefrontsize()` disagrees with `kWaveSize`.\n\nCDNA (`__GFX9__`) keeps `kWaveSize = 64`, so the gfx942/gfx950 code is unchanged.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nAOT kernel unit tests, one pytest per file, built with `AMDGPU_TARGET` set to the GPU under test:\n\n| test | gfx1100 before | gfx1100 after | gfx1201 before | gfx1201 after | gfx950 after |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| test_topk | **157 failed, 5 passed** | 162 passed, 1 skipped | **157 failed, 5 passed** | 162 passed, 1 skipped | 162 passed, 1 skipped (same as before) |\n| test_moe_topk_softmax | 744 passed | 744 passed | 744 passed | 744 passed | 744 passed |\n| test_moe_topk_sigmoid | 774 passed | 774 passed | 774 passed | 774 passed | |\n| test_activation | 945 passed | 945 passed | 945 passed | 945 passed | |\n| test_dsv4_norm_rope | 16 passed | 16 passed | 16 passed | 16 passed | |\n| test_moe_align | 4368 passed, 72 skipped | 4368 passed, 72 skipped | 4368 passed, 72 skipped | 4368 passed, 72 skipped | |\n\nEnvironment: ROCm 7.2.x with PyTorch 2.10. gfx1100 is a Radeon PRO W7900D, gfx1201 a Radeon AI PRO R9700, and gfx950 an MI355X.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nN/A for RDNA (correctness fix). On CDNA the kernels are unchanged apart from a `check_wave_size()` that folds to nothing on wave64 targets, as on `main`.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [x] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests). (Covered by the existing `tests/test_topk.py`.)\n- [x] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations). (No doc change needed.)\n- [x] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results. (See above.)\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #40617563197](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40617563197)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #40617563251](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40617563251)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #40617563198](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40617563198)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
